    {
      "id": "1573075713266032863",
      "type": "Reply",
      "timestamp": "2026-11-19T20:41:16.376+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "Notably for a target ball size and pitch that works with regular FR4-laminate PCB's. I assume with \"only\" via-in-pad, not really need for HDI/blind vias.\nThe JLC flip chip process I'm referring to would be with presumably ACF or _theoretically_ ENIG/ENEPIG grown-pillars undergoing gold-to-gold \"compliant bonding\" where you basically just skip the ACF and maybe throw in a lil ultrasonic action with the hot compression. If it works and doesn't rip off, I'd expect _that_ to have superior electrical properties and electrical consistency&reliability.",
      "author": {
        "id": "262706220073222144",
        "name": "namibj",
        "discriminator": "0000",
        "nickname": "namibj",
        "color": null,
        "isBot": false,
        "roles": [],
        "avatarUrl": "2026-11_media/f885abc0dddd0a33e4d4991b3c99091d-7ACD2.png"
